+### Optional browser interaction check
+
+If Chromium or Chrome is already installed, this separate smoke check uses only
+Node built-ins and the browser debugging pipe (no npm packages or server):
+
+```sh
+node scripts/check-html-browser.js /path/to/chromium
+```
+
+It checks native Tab/Enter/Space interactions, accessible disclosure names and
+states, visible keyboard focus, desktop/narrow layouts, and literal rendering of
+hostile markup. It also captures three PNG previews in a temporary directory
+printed on success. An optional second argument chooses the screenshot directory
+(existing files with the same screenshot names are overwritten). It uses an
+isolated temporary browser profile and removes that profile afterward.
+
+The browser sandbox stays enabled by default. Only when running inside an already
+isolated container that cannot launch Chromium otherwise, set
+`CHROME_NO_SANDBOX=1` for this smoke check. A browser is not needed to run
+`node --test` or generate reports.
